      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_6818_*|*_3_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i003yf:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Seriously consider Set<T> having",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tChange EqualsComparer to EqualComparerType (function<bool(T,T)>) and DefaultEqualsComparer",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tReview implications for inherited methods from Iterable<>",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tReview implications for sorted comparisns (subclasses sortedset).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tReview implications for commutatitivty)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tConsider if I can do this ONLY for Set<>/SortedSet<> - just as a way to get started, and if works well, do for Mapping etc.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "\tDo all work in backend. Just extra param to CTOR. Then backend does the rest. Not sure we want to bother with TRAITS for Set<>. Simpler without, and the only thing used to replace is comparer, and that’s better replaced by CTOR ARG.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "USE",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/equal_to"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/equal_to",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "instead of my usual compare crap",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "and ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/less"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/less",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "and I THIUNK – test this",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "using EqualsComparerType  std::function<bool(const T&,const T&)>;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "void WebService::Server::ExpectedMethod (const Request* request, const Set<String>& methods, const Optional<String>& fromInMessage)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "{",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "String method{request->GetHTTPMethod ()};",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// @todo rewrite to do better case insensitive compare",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Iterable<String> lcMethods = methods.Select<String> ([](const String& s) { return s.ToLowerCase ();  });",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "if (not methods.Contains (method.ToLowerCase ())) {",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Execution::Throw (",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Execution::StringException (",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Characters::Format (L\"Got HTTP method %s%s, but expected one from %s\", Characters::ToString (method).c_str (), (fromInMessage ? (L\" from \" + *fromInMessage) : L\"\").c_str (), Characters::ToString (methods).c_str ())",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "));",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "}",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "}",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
